{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that order the minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanning forest is unique, and this is it. Its edges are listed in nondecreasing weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and, among equal weights, in position order, and the weight is added up in that order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}]}],"name":"Complexity"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not overflow and is not NaN."}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L21","fileName":"Kruskal.swift"},"title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/s